Private experiment executor/judge. Never imported by the consumer.

Restored arms share exact initial body, coupling and external schedule;
only the intended action differs. Body and schedules stay in audit traces.

Bounded observed encounter history in the agent's existing CAM.

No policy, other-mind access or parallel episodic store. Facts are receipts;
summaries are derived queries and never promoted to factual predictions.

Finite token grammar for model-authored bounded control strategies (S6-B2).

Values and conditions are selected by model probabilities. Syntax is fixed;
no candidate is selected, repaired, or ranked using game results here.

Controls on the same recorded observations and budgets. None is ever flown.

- horizon one and reactive Q: decision replay on the flight's own observations
  (first divergence and whether the control's proposal would pass the gates),
  plus COMPOSE-1's functional twin on the same room geometry;
- fixed battery percentage: POWER-1's `fixed` Guard on the recorded battery;
- a link that takes the ACK as arrival: the gateway mutant replayed on the
  recorded ACK/telemetry stream, judged against the private pose at ACK time;
- gate ablations: an agent without evidence gating, and SAFE without agent
  liveness or without the latch, replayed on the recorded inputs.

Bytes first, structure second.

Every hash SIM-3 publishes is over bytes that exist on disk, taken before
anything parses them. Every canonical form is a byte string with a fixed
recipe, so an auditor can rebuild it without trusting our parser.

Rules that are easy to get wrong and are therefore enforced here:

* a file larger than ``MAX_FILE_BYTES`` is refused before it is read into
  a parser at all;
* duplicate JSON keys are an error, not a last-one-wins;
* ``NaN``/``Infinity`` are an error, in both directions;
* a path inside a package may not escape it, and may not be a symlink.

Offline, resumable V3 batch evaluation. No LLM, learning or automatic submission.

prepare separates public inputs from labels; workers receive only public inputs;
grading happens in the parent after each fresh solver process has exited.

Publishable charts and 3D tree GIFs derived from verified capacity evidence.

Rendering is outside measurement. Tree positions and animation speed are visual;
indices, weights, scores and program outputs are reconstructed and checked.

Additive ARC grid candidate: 3E receipts, cached synthesis and bounded views.

No test outputs are consumed. All arms share the same executed-program budget;
primitive work, cache use and memory retrieval are separately recorded.

V2 development candidate: relation-first residual synthesis and depth allocation.

No test outputs are consumed. All arms share the same executed-program budget;
primitive work, cache use and memory retrieval are separately recorded.

GUI-4 tests.

These guard the contract in ``docs/GUI4-DESIGN.md``, not the pixels:

* custody: no new file under ``nexus0/``, no pinned file touched;
* observer: the renderer never mutates the snapshot it is handed;
* origin: every case and every exported figure declares where it came from;
* catalogue: no orphan case, and a blocked case explains itself;
* bench: real contrasts with a visible denominator and traceable export.
